Linebacker, David Bowens let the ball escape because of Warner.
At the last change, the loss of Bowens' balloon, may well be the most charming event
The Cardinals took control of this possession for the last 10 seconds, and then the Jets recovered the ball, Jay Feely made a 20-yard goal taking an advantage from 34-0.
It was the best that the Jets were able to score in a time.
"Jets coach Eric Mangini, who was asked to describe this madness, said "the second or the third?"
When he was told the two--the Jets dropped 21 undisputable points in the third time – Mangini said: “I can tell you that I enjoyed the second time more than the third.
